  "question": {
    "text": "In an examination, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> students have been allotted their seats as per their roll numbers. The number of ways, in which none of the students sits on the allotted seat, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "44",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;boys with allotted roll numbers and seat numbers are seated in such a way that no one sits on the allotted seats. The number of ways of such seating arrangement is equal to the derangement of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;boys i.e.,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>44</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
